  "findings": [
    "Native efficacy, exposure, fidelity/norm numerators and denominators match frozen summary and audit summary; no arithmetic discrepancy in requested quantities.",
    "All six native efficacy medians pass both signs on each historical split, but every sign/split fails fidelity and each split fails exposure for feature 22004. No engineering or behavioral assay qualification.",
    "Neighbor count medians conditional on requested edits are 199 suppression and 215/214 amplification, versus zero across all positions. Counts do not by themselves establish semantic or behavioral harm.",
    "Selected-width suppression is unavailable for calibration 58667 and 41533 and validation 30686 because each contains one zero selected_before at a native-active position. Its valid-subset median remains near 0.251; do not present unavailable decisions as evidence of ineffective suppression.",
    "Three historical native target-coordinate differences across 84150 entries prevent exact historical replay wording; no target support or exposure change. FP32 differences remain within stated tolerance.",
    "Previously observed splits, token-weighted descriptive medians and sparse 22004 exposure do not establish fresh generalization, feature selectivity, downstream NLL preservation, behavioral positive-control response, headroom, or consciousness outcomes."
  ],
  "headline": "On 544 saved states, the A40 full-width native SAE measurements meet the six conditional efficacy thresholds at the fixed 4% continuous norm cap, with all realized nonzero edits under the 5% limit; delivery fidelity and rare-feature exposure still fail, so this demonstrates median coordinate efficacy on saved states, not a qualified behavioral assay.",
  "notes": [
    "The initial selected-width cross-check compared finite-subset medians to conservative whole-set decision medians. Checking the saved ratio.median and undefined_positions separately resolved the difference; the null decision medians are intentional, not arithmetic errors.",
    "Source row file hashes were checked; capture hash identifiers were matched to plan but residual capture file bytes were not independently hashed or loaded.",
    "Only the permitted independent JSON is written. Parent owns final documentation, plot and release work."
